	(text "152 mA for 200 ms every 10 s (3 mA avg)\nonly while the board draws less than\nthe bank's threshold. Firmware setting\ncan turn it off; R12 DNP = hard off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 238.76 261.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "61c3116c-f199-5624-811b-5c671f7c4154")
	)
	(text "VSENSE = VOUT / 13: 27.7 V (OVP) -> 2.13 V, inside the C3's\nADC range at 11 dB. Firmware uses it for:\n - P_LED = VOUT x I_set, capped at 5 W\n - open string or reversed filament (VOUT > 25.5 V, near OVP): EN off, retry\n - shorted output (VOUT ~ 0 while lit)\n - each start: 10 % current first, VOUT checked against the learned window\n - what is connected (one 12 V ~ 11 V, 3 x 3 V ~ 8.4 V)\n0 uA when the driver is off (C4 blocks DC).\nR26-R28: 1 k series on the radar lines (ESD on the cable/socket)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 256.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "66e48ad8-a57f-575f-b2f4-ef51ab289bfc")
	)
	(text "5  POT + POWER SWITCH, RADAR (SOCKET OR PIGTAIL)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.97 204.47 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "85c7ef17-e80e-59da-9f81-183073668653")
	)
	(text "D4 feeds the XIAO's 5V pin and blocks back-feed from its own USB-C.\nD6 (GPIO21) is UART0 TX: it toggles during boot, so ISEL goes through R22.\nD7 (GPIO20, UART0 RX) drives EN. GPIO20 has a ~45 k pull-up at reset, so R18 is\n2.2 k: EN stays below 0.4 V until the firmware drives it (also in download mode).\nD8 (GPIO8) reads JP2, pulled up by R29 (10 k): low = manual mode\n(radar ignored). Strapping pin, but only in download mode: move the\nshunt off 1-2 before forcing download with BOOT. D0/D9 unconnected. J9/J10: 5 mm low-profile sockets\n(JLCPCB fits them); the XIAO's USB-C faces the board edge."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50.8 182.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "939a85bb-8890-51c9-bdf5-1766b5c87acc")
	)
	(text "6  STRING VOLTAGE SENSE, RADAR LINE RESISTORS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 158.75 207.01 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "968cc087-e074-5451-bec1-f65466001687")
	)
	(text "Power: 5 V from the bank via Q2. LED power capped at 5 W in firmware\n(~1.4 A from the bank); 1.7 W lit at prototype brightness; idle ~4 mA\nwith keep-alive, ~0.7 mA without (model: power_model.py).\n\nPins (XIAO):\n  D1 GPIO3  ADC_POT    ADC1_CH3\n  D2 GPIO4  VSENSE     ADC1_CH4, VOUT / 13\n  D3 GPIO5  RADAR_OT2  wake, high = present\n  D4 GPIO6  UART_TX -> radar RX (115200 8N1)\n  D5 GPIO7  UART_RX <- radar OT1/TX\n  D6 GPIO21 ISEL_IO    low = 244 mA (shunt 2-3), via R22\n  D7 GPIO20 DIM_PWM    LEDC 19.5 kHz -> EN (analog dim)\n  D8 GPIO8  RADAR_MODE   JP2 1-2 = manual, 2-3/none = radar\n  D10 GPIO10 KA_DRV    keep-alive gate\n\nAssembly: JLCPCB fits everything incl. through-hole J2-J8 and the\nXIAO sockets; you plug in the XIAO and the radar. DNP: D1.\n\nBring-up (docs/g2_decisions.md): SEPIC at the extremes (one 3 V\nfilament at 244 mA; 24 V string at the 5 W cap), filament\ntemperature in the frame, bank wake via the switch."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 309.88 29.21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "af82b0b3-58c4-5585-a850-330acd4a4cd4")
	)
	(text "SEPIC: +5V -> L1 -> SW (switch) ; C4 couples SW to SEP_B ; L2 SEP_B -> GND ;\nD5 SEP_B -> VOUT. Works for any string from one 3 V filament (~2.7 V) to 24 V,\nand C4 blocks DC: no current path from the bank to the LEDs when U2 is off.\nf = 1.17 MHz (R19 82 k). OVP = 1.229 x (1 + 110k/5.1k) = 27.7 V (29.1 V worst case);\nswitch sees VIN + VOUT + VD <= 35.1 V worst case (40 V abs max). L1 = L2 = 10 uH, 4.1 A sat.\nC5 is 100 V (X7S 1210) so it keeps its capacitance and > 2x margin at OVP.\nDimming: 19.5 kHz PWM on EN, filtered inside U2 by DIMC (C7) -> analog FB reference,\nI_LED = duty x I_max. EN low > 10 ms = shutdown (2 uA). R18 (2.2 k) holds EN below 0.4 V\nagainst GPIO20's ~45 k reset pull-up, so U2 stays off through boot and USB flashing.\nCOMP C9 100 nF. Lowest RHPZ 43 kHz (5 W into a 12 V string, 4.5 V in): keep crossover\n< 4.3 kHz. SLVA904 measured 1.7 kHz with 15 nF / 4.7 uH; 100 nF / 10 uH is lower still.\nTune 15-470 nF on the bench. Checks: sepic_design.py (switch peak 2.2 A vs 3 A min)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 309.88 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b7c9eec5-a645-543b-b63d-a9a6a4fd67c1")
	)
	(text "Fill ports in order from PORT 1. Each filament: + wire -> its port's +, - wire -> NEXT,\nexcept the LAST filament's - wire -> END (PORT 4's NEXT is END too). Longest string 24 V.\nWIRE PORTS ONLY WITH THE POWER SWITCH OFF: an open string holds VOUT near OVP.\nOpen or reversed filament: VOUT near OVP, firmware turns U2 off and retries at low current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 171.45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c3d4d0c2-c0c2-5ce1-802c-86c132a6f867")
	)
	(text "NOTES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 308.61 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ca741686-fd89-529f-b58b-6011d7038afb")
	)
	(text "I_max = 0.2 V / Rs. JP1 is a 2.54 mm\nheader with one shunt:\n 2-3: R20 only, 244 mA; ISEL low.\n 1-2: R21 in parallel, 488 mA;\n      ISEL high (R23).\n none: 244 mA; ISEL high, so the\n      firmware assumes 488 and\n      under-drives (safe)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.38 184.15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d2fabdde-cabf-5b9d-8692-5314e5c7588f")
	)
	(text "4  MCU: SEEED XIAO ESP32C3 IN 5 mm SOCKETS (bought with pins)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.97 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e20b9458-3e6f-55f4-a98d-eb646134f5bf")
	)
	(text "J2: pot with built-in switch, off at the CCW stop. Numbered like the pot:\n1 CCW end + switch common (GND), 2 wiper, 3 CW end, 4 switch (SW_N). CW = brighter.\nWiper 0-2.24 V (47 k + 100 k pot). R6/C12 ESD + sampling filter.\nJ3 (radar plugs in directly) and J4 (radar on a cable) are in parallel,\n1:1 with the LD2410S header: 3V3, GND, OT1/TX, RX, OT2. Use one.\nFB1/C13/C14 keep switching noise off the radar supply."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 264.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e2fb6dd3-0e81-5975-a328-e2be90ce9203")
	)
	(text "Power switch: the pot's switch (J2 pin 4) pulls SW_N to GND.\n ON:  Rd (R1/R2 5.1 k) reach GND, so a USB-C bank sees a sink attach and\n      turns VBUS on; Q2's gate goes low and Q2 connects VBUS_F to +5V.\n OFF: Rd float (bank sees nothing attached, sleeps) and R13 holds Q2 off,\n      which also cuts non-compliant banks and USB-A to C cables.\nSoft start: R14 10 k with C16 100 nF ramps Q2's gate over ~1 ms, so\n+5V charges at ~0.2 A instead of an amps-level spike. R14 also keeps\ncable ESD off the gate. The switch carries < 0.5 mA.\nF1: 1.5 A hold / 3 A trip. Max normal draw 1.4 A (5 W LED cap).\nD1 DNP. Bring-up test G2-T6 (live USB-A plug-in) checks the XIAO 5V pin stays <= 6.0 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50.8 82.55 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e7d5d80a-caa7-5987-99c8-05d19077dcaa")
	)
